---
import { MCP_FEATURE_PATH, SCOPES, TOOL_REFERENCE_PATH } from '@lib/solutions/engineering-teams';
---

<section class="border-t border-line" aria-labelledby="et-asyou-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="et-asyou-title" class="h2">
        The agent works as you, never around you.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5 max-w-[46ch]">
        Every write an agent makes happens under the token of the person who connected it, with that person’s
        permissions. It can never do more than their role allows, the token’s scopes can narrow it further, and each
        change lands in the activity log under their name.
      </p>
      <p class="prose mt-4 max-w-[46ch]">
        The MCP server calls the same public API as the web app. Deleting something, or changing roles and access, stops
        and asks the person in their agent app before anything happens.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href={TOOL_REFERENCE_PATH}>
          Check every tool and what it changes
          <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
            →
          </span>
        </a>
        <a class="link" href={MCP_FEATURE_PATH}>
          MCP and AI agents
          <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
            →
          </span>
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-6 lg:col-start-7 min-w-0">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-medium">Scopes a developer’s token might hold</h3>
      <dl class="scopes mt-3">
        {SCOPES.map(item => (
          <>
            <dt>
              <code>{item.scope}</code>
            </dt>
            <dd>{item.lets}</dd>
          </>
        ))}
      </dl>
      <p class="prose text-base mt-6">
        A refusal is real. When the role allows an action but the token does not, the answer names the missing scope:
      </p>
      <p class="quote mt-3">This access token does not have the time:write scope</p>
      <p class="prose text-base mt-6">
        The tool reference marks each tool <em>Reads only</em> or <em>Changes data</em>, so a team can decide which
        scopes an agent gets before it connects.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
